WEBVTT

00:02.335 --> 00:04.098
I think what Mac's trying to say...

00:04.170 --> 00:06.104
is that it's probably
the greatest movie of all time.

00:06.172 --> 00:07.969
That's 'cause it is.

00:08.041 --> 00:09.531
Rocky IV is not
the greatest movie of all time.

00:09.609 --> 00:11.076
Dee, what do you consider
to be a good movie?

00:11.144 --> 00:13.374
- I don't know, like, Million Dollar Baby...
- Oh, come on.

00:13.446 --> 00:17.007
- Are you kidding me? That is ridiculous.
- Come on. It won an Oscar.

00:17.083 --> 00:19.017
Rocky IV has Stallone in it...

00:19.085 --> 00:21.144
and he bashes a Russian's face
to all smithereens.

00:21.221 --> 00:23.883
Lifting anvils and shit,
and pulling trucks through the snow.

00:23.957 --> 00:25.891
Million Dollar Baby
is totally unrealistic.

00:25.959 --> 00:27.950
- Girls can't fight. They don't have muscles.
- It's true.

00:28.028 --> 00:30.553
Okay, that is a horribly sexist thing to say.

00:30.630 --> 00:32.564
It's not sexist.
It's just truthful.

00:32.632 --> 00:34.566
Girls can't pull trucks through snow.

00:34.634 --> 00:36.602
- Can you pull trucks through snow?
- I absolutely could.

00:36.669 --> 00:38.762
- You can barely walk in the snow.
- Excuse me.

00:38.838 --> 00:41.102
Time out. Is the truck parked in neutral?

00:41.174 --> 00:43.734
- Hey!
- What, dude?

00:43.810 --> 00:46.438
Empty your pockets.

00:47.514 --> 00:50.176
- Now.
- Okay.

00:50.250 --> 00:53.686
Hey, let's just all stay calm.

00:59.659 --> 01:01.593
Nice friends.

01:33.593 --> 01:37.256
Maybe... one to two inches of snow?

01:37.330 --> 01:40.299
- One to two inches...
- And a Ford F-150.

01:40.366 --> 01:43.130
Right. In park, but no emergency brake.

01:43.203 --> 01:46.263
Maybe I could pull it four feet.

01:46.339 --> 01:49.775
- I'd give him four feet.
- I'd give him five. What's with the gym bag?

01:49.843 --> 01:52.573
Just got back from
a "Boxercise" class at the gym.

01:52.645 --> 01:56.012
"Boxercise"? What kind
of queer shit is that?

01:56.082 --> 02:00.542
- I'm learning self-defense.
- You wanna learn self-defense, you come to Daddy.

02:00.620 --> 02:03.851
I mean, all during the '60s, before
I met my whore wife, I was a boxer.

02:03.923 --> 02:05.857
They called me Frankie Fast Hands.

02:05.925 --> 02:08.758
Frankie Fast Hands, everybody.
Yeah, keep livin' in the past, Dad.

02:08.828 --> 02:12.491
Is this about that stupid
Million Dollar Baby movie, Dee?

02:12.565 --> 02:14.726
No, actually, Mac,
it's about being left with a mugger...

02:14.801 --> 02:17.031
because my chickenshit brother
and his friends ditched me.

02:17.103 --> 02:19.128
- You ditched your sister?
- Absolutely.

02:19.205 --> 02:21.139
- With a mugger...
- The guy had a knife.

02:21.207 --> 02:23.437
Of course we did.
What were we supposed to do?

02:23.510 --> 02:26.308
If I was there, I would have used
my Frankie Fast Hands technique.

02:26.379 --> 02:28.643
Technique don't mean shit
out on the streets. Guys have knives.

02:28.715 --> 02:31.548
Yeah. In boxing, there are rules.
On the streets, we ain't got no rules.

02:31.618 --> 02:33.552
Ain't no rules out on the streets.

02:33.620 --> 02:36.714
- You guys got no rules on the streets, you.
- Oh, please.

02:36.789 --> 02:38.757
Will you stop talking
about the streets...

02:38.825 --> 02:40.793
you three jackasses,
like you've been there?

02:40.860 --> 02:45.729
I mean, any underground street fight in
Philadelphia, you'd find tons of technique.

02:45.798 --> 02:49.359
- You think you could teach me?
- In a month I'll have you kicking all their asses.

02:49.435 --> 02:51.460
Right. See you then.

02:51.538 --> 02:53.529
Dennis, I have an idea.

02:59.712 --> 03:02.180
- Well, this is awesome.
- Yeah. This is amazing.

03:02.248 --> 03:04.182
There's blood everywhere. It's beautiful.

03:04.250 --> 03:06.718
Yeah, and we were totally right.
These guys don't have technique.

03:06.786 --> 03:09.812
They get all cranked up like animals
and beat the Christ out of each other.

03:09.889 --> 03:11.823
Look at all this money
being thrown around.

03:11.891 --> 03:15.190
- Dude, we gotta get in on this.
- Oh, yeah.

03:15.261 --> 03:17.695
- Really, I think it's about who can take the biggest beating.
- Yeah.

03:17.764 --> 03:20.426
Get up!

03:20.500 --> 03:22.434
You know who can take
a really good beating?

03:22.502 --> 03:23.935
- Charlie.
- Charlie.

03:25.672 --> 03:28.368
Here she is... The old gym.

03:28.441 --> 03:30.375
Smell that?

03:30.443 --> 03:33.606
- That's the smell of hard work.
- And feet.

03:33.680 --> 03:37.377
That's the smell of big dreams.
The smell of glory.

03:37.450 --> 03:40.613
- It smells like feet.
- And feet. Does smell like feet.

03:40.687 --> 03:43.281
- Frank?
- Oh, shit.

03:43.356 --> 03:45.415
Frankie Fast Hands!

03:45.491 --> 03:48.790
- Holy crap. I knew it was you.
I haven't seen you in years.

03:48.861 --> 03:52.388
Hey-Hey-Hey, Frankie, it's me.
Bobby Thunderson.

03:52.465 --> 03:54.558
- Yes. Yes. Yes, Bobby.
- Look at you!

03:54.634 --> 03:57.102
You... really let yourself go.

03:57.170 --> 03:59.798
Oh-Oh, are you trying
to get back into fighting form?

03:59.872 --> 04:03.467
No, I'm actually, uh, teaching
my daughter some self-defense.

04:03.543 --> 04:06.171
Holy... Holy shit, man.
I'm training my daughter too.

04:06.246 --> 04:09.909
Hey, what do you know? Hey, look at her.
Look at her over there.

04:09.983 --> 04:13.043
Look, look, look. Oh!

04:13.119 --> 04:15.314
Amazing. Hey, she's pretty too, huh?

04:15.388 --> 04:17.754
Like her old man, huh?

04:17.824 --> 04:19.985
- Well, it's really nice seeing you, Bob.
- Yeah.

04:20.059 --> 04:22.254
Hey, don't listen
to everything this guy tells you.

04:22.328 --> 04:24.819
You don't wanna get knocked out
in the first round.

04:24.897 --> 04:27.457
Oh, my God, that's
an annoying sound he makes.

04:27.533 --> 04:29.763
- Ass... hole.
- Yeah, asshole.

04:29.836 --> 04:32.600
Okay, don't listen to anything he says.
He's a real creep.

04:32.672 --> 04:35.300
All right, now. Here, we're gonna
start weight training.

04:35.375 --> 04:38.139
First things first... Squats.

04:40.346 --> 04:42.746
Okay. That's it.

04:42.815 --> 04:44.749
Uh, that looks really heavy.

04:44.817 --> 04:47.342
Look. This is not gonna be
a half-assed workout.

04:47.420 --> 04:49.581
We gotta really get into it.
It's gonna hurt.

04:49.656 --> 04:53.854
- Yeah, but I can't lift that.
- Just position yourself under the bar and listen to me.

04:53.926 --> 04:56.861
Here's what you're gonna do.
You're gonna take all the weight on your neck.

04:56.929 --> 05:01.332
Then you're gonna jam your legs down
and hyperextend your ankles...

05:01.401 --> 05:04.802
and then shoot back up
and lock your knees in place.

05:06.072 --> 05:09.200
Not one of those things
sounds right to me at all.

05:09.275 --> 05:10.902
Look. You wanna fight like a man?

05:10.977 --> 05:14.538
You gotta train like a man.
Now, come on. Gimme a squat.

05:14.614 --> 05:17.242
- Ready. Go!
- Oh, my God!

05:17.317 --> 05:19.308
- Go. Keep it up.
- Daddy, I can't.

05:19.385 --> 05:22.081
- It's... I can't.
- Keep it up. Keep it up.

05:23.990 --> 05:27.187
At least I got the one. Right?

05:27.260 --> 05:29.251
Yeah. Get out, get out, get out.

05:32.265 --> 05:34.233
We got a lot of work to do.

05:34.300 --> 05:37.064
Good, good.

05:37.136 --> 05:39.070
- Ah!
- Mm-hmm.

05:39.138 --> 05:41.470
What are we doing?

05:41.541 --> 05:43.566
Charlie, you're, like,
the toughest guy we know.

05:43.643 --> 05:45.770
- Yeah?
- So nobody can kick your ass, right?

05:45.845 --> 05:47.779
- Practically invincible.
- Yeah.

05:47.847 --> 05:49.781
Yeah, what's your point though?

05:49.849 --> 05:51.976
Well... So here's what's gonna happen, pal.

05:52.051 --> 05:54.542
Dennis and I are gonna train you...

05:54.620 --> 05:57.054
to be an underground street fighter.

05:57.123 --> 05:59.114
What? That is brilliant.

05:59.192 --> 06:01.820
- Yeah, it is.
- Okay, what's the first step?

06:01.894 --> 06:04.727
- First step is getting that shirt off.
- Yeah, let's get that shirt off.

06:04.797 --> 06:07.322
- Why would I do that?
- That shirt's just gonna weigh you down.

06:07.400 --> 06:09.368
Yeah, and Rocky never
wears a shirt when he trains...

06:09.435 --> 06:11.665
so let's just go ahead
and rip that bad boy off.

06:11.738 --> 06:14.434
I think I'm gonna wear it.

06:14.507 --> 06:17.169
That's ridiculous.
You can't train and wear a shirt, dude.

06:17.243 --> 06:20.007
Now it's becoming this
whole big thing. It feels a little gay.

06:20.079 --> 06:22.172
- It's not gay. Just take your shirt off.
- It's not gay.

06:22.248 --> 06:26.241
Why can't I just get, like, all excited and
passionately rip it off in the moment?

06:26.319 --> 06:29.948
- Why can't you just take your shirt off for us?
- Just drop it for now.

06:30.022 --> 06:32.252
All right, all right.
Uh, maybe you should punch something.

06:32.325 --> 06:34.759
- There you go.
- Yeah, you should punch something...

06:34.827 --> 06:36.727
Why don't you punch this board?

06:36.796 --> 06:38.957
Okay. Hold it steady for me.

06:39.031 --> 06:41.192
- Watch your eyes.
- All right, come on.

06:41.267 --> 06:43.201
Oh!

06:43.269 --> 06:45.635
Oh, that's...

06:45.705 --> 06:47.935
- That looks like it stings.
- Oh, my God.

06:48.007 --> 06:51.340
- What's that made out of?
- It's a board, so it's, you know, made out of wood.

06:51.411 --> 06:53.606
- It's, like, particle board.
- It's, like, harder than wood, dude.

06:53.679 --> 06:55.613
- No.
- It's actually softer than wood.

06:55.681 --> 06:58.013
- Yeah, it's a lot softer than wood.
- Petrified wood.

06:58.084 --> 07:00.109
- What happened, man? I thought you were...
- I don't know.

07:00.186 --> 07:02.211
- I wasn't drunk enough.
- You should be drunk for this.

07:02.288 --> 07:04.586
- We should all be drunk for this.
- Let's get really drunk.

07:04.657 --> 07:06.682
- All right.
- Yeah. You know what? I'll get some beers.

07:06.759 --> 07:08.693
- Come with me.
- Wait, wait, wait, wait.

07:08.761 --> 07:10.695
Let him go.

07:14.867 --> 07:16.801
- Mmm.
- I don't know what happened.

07:16.869 --> 07:20.270
- Mmm. Mmm.
- Mmm.

07:22.809 --> 07:25.903
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Deandra,
we've been at this for days now.

07:25.978 --> 07:28.242
It's like you have no motor skills.

07:28.314 --> 07:32.307
Just grab that bar
and jerk it down behind your neck.

07:32.385 --> 07:34.785
Hey! How's the chip
off the old block doin'?

07:34.854 --> 07:38.756
- Bobby, not now, okay?
- Hey, your old man ever tell you how we fought back in '61?

07:38.825 --> 07:41.919
They billed it as "Beauty Versus the Beast."

07:41.994 --> 07:44.053
Wasn't much of a fight.
First-round knockout.

07:44.130 --> 07:46.291
- He went down like a...
- Wait, wait, wait.

07:46.365 --> 07:48.765
Hold on a second.
What's goin' on with you, Thunderson?

07:48.835 --> 07:50.826
What, are you trying
to humiliate me?

07:50.903 --> 07:53.599
Uh, I think you did that
to yourself 40 years ago.

07:53.673 --> 07:56.267
You know damn well
you hit me after the bell.

07:56.342 --> 07:59.368
- That was a cheap shot.
- What are you... You know, excuses are like assholes.

07:59.445 --> 08:01.379
Everybody's got one,
and they all stink.

08:01.447 --> 08:03.881
- Oh, yeah? You wanna go at it right now?
- Whoa, whoa, whoa.

08:03.950 --> 08:06.077
You wanna settle this now?
Let's do it right here.

08:06.152 --> 08:08.086
Let's settle this son of a bitch right here.

08:08.154 --> 08:11.146
Hey, hey. Take it easy here.
Jesus. Show a little class, will ya?

08:11.224 --> 08:14.057
Geez. Look, I'm an old man.
I don't fight no more.

08:14.126 --> 08:16.219
I let my daughter
do my fighting for me.

08:16.295 --> 08:19.230
And maybe in a couple years,
when this little graham cracker...

08:19.298 --> 08:21.994
might have the stuff to compete,
maybe we'll see.

08:22.068 --> 08:24.832
Wait. You know what, asshole?
Why don't you go to hell?

08:24.904 --> 08:28.840
- Dee, stay out of this.
- No. This guy has been all over us since we walked in.

08:28.908 --> 08:30.842
I tell you what, jerk.
Why don't you take you big mouth...

08:30.910 --> 08:32.844
and go someplace else with it?

08:32.912 --> 08:35.403
Listen, little buttercup,
I'm just bustin' your old man's balls.

08:35.481 --> 08:38.075
- You don't have to get your panties in an uproar.
- Oh, my God.

08:38.150 --> 08:40.414
Are you standing there?
Come on, move.

08:40.486 --> 08:43.751
- That guy is such an asshole.
- Don't blame it on him.

08:43.823 --> 08:47.589
You're not makin' any progress.
I'm goin' to get the jump rope.

08:50.162 --> 08:53.893
- Men are such pricks.
- Oh, tell me about it.

08:53.966 --> 08:56.628
I bet you're real tired
of them pushing you around.

08:56.702 --> 08:58.636
Oh, God, you have no idea.

08:58.704 --> 09:01.195
If only there was a way
that you could be...

09:01.274 --> 09:04.402
physically tough enough
to intimidate men.

09:04.477 --> 09:07.002
I'm sorry. Do I know you?

09:07.079 --> 09:10.742
Let's just say I provide
a much-needed service around this place.

09:10.816 --> 09:14.752
Step into the shadows
and, uh, we'll talk.

09:15.821 --> 09:18.483
Yeah?

09:18.558 --> 09:21.891
Mac and Dennis, dude. Open the door.

09:21.961 --> 09:24.828
- What?
- It's Mac and Dennis. Open the door.

09:24.897 --> 09:26.831
Open the door, bro.

09:26.899 --> 09:29.026
All right, guys.
Hang on a second. It's like, uh...

09:29.101 --> 09:31.569
It's like 11:00 in the morning here.

09:31.637 --> 09:33.571
- We don't care. Open the door.
- Surprise, bitch.

09:33.639 --> 09:38.133
You're hittin' me with that?

09:38.210 --> 09:40.269
Charlie, let's be honest.
Punching boards isn't your thing.

09:40.346 --> 09:42.576
- But that's okay.
- Yes, that's okay, because for you...

09:42.648 --> 09:44.741
it's not gonna be about
inflicting punishment...

09:44.817 --> 09:47.650
it's gonna be about having
punishment inflicted upon you.

09:47.720 --> 09:50.154
- We need to smash things all over your body.
- Yes!

09:50.222 --> 09:52.156
- No.
- Yes.

09:52.224 --> 09:54.692
- We need to build up your tolerance to beatings.
- Hence the smashing.

09:54.760 --> 09:57.957
- We used a trash can, but Dennis wanted to use a chair.
- I think he's ready.

09:58.030 --> 10:00.055
- That's way too excessive at this point.
- That guy's ready.

10:00.132 --> 10:02.225
- He's not ready for a chair.
- I'm tellin' you, he's ready.

10:02.301 --> 10:04.735
Hey! Guys! I can handle a chair.
Go get a chair.

10:04.804 --> 10:07.238
See what you're doing to him?
You're getting him all worked up.

10:07.306 --> 10:10.070
- He's the toughest guy we know.
- Yes, he is, but he...

10:10.142 --> 10:12.838
Hey, Mac! Get a chair,
smash it on my back.

10:12.912 --> 10:15.574
That's the right attitude.
He's got the right attitude.

10:15.648 --> 10:19.948
I'll tell you what. Charlie, go put on
those little short-shorts.

10:20.019 --> 10:21.953
- Let's take things to the next level.
- Yeah.

10:22.021 --> 10:24.615
- But first things first. Let's get good and drunk.
- Let's get drunk!

10:27.426 --> 10:29.417
- Whoa!
- Whoa! Whoo!

10:29.495 --> 10:32.487
Drink this. Drink this.

10:35.834 --> 10:38.928
Now, just to be clear,
these aren't steroids, right?

10:39.004 --> 10:40.938
No, no, no, no.
Of course not.

10:41.006 --> 10:43.702
These are performance-enhancing supplements.

10:43.776 --> 10:46.643
Okay, so how long before
I start to notice something?

10:46.712 --> 10:49.476
This is the good stuff.
You'll feel it almost immediately.

10:49.548 --> 10:52.813
But I should warn you,
you may experience some mood swings...

10:52.885 --> 10:54.819
some irrational thinking
here and there...

10:54.887 --> 10:57.583
but it is nothing compared
to the long-term effects.

10:57.656 --> 11:01.456
- Which are what?
- You ever punched a guy so hard in the eye he swallowed it?

11:01.527 --> 11:04.394
I'll get some water.

11:04.463 --> 11:07.432
- How you feel, man? You drunk?
- Yeah. I'm pretty wasted.

11:07.499 --> 11:09.967
- Great. So what do we smash first?
- I wanna smash a crate.

11:10.035 --> 11:12.162
- Yeah, a crate on his back.
- Why don't you punch me?

11:12.237 --> 11:14.228
- Punch you? Punch you?
- What?

11:14.306 --> 11:16.501
I'm probably gonna get punched a lot
in the tournament, right?

11:16.575 --> 11:18.509
- Yeah. All right.
- Okay, that's a good point.

11:18.577 --> 11:20.670
- Let's punch him.
- Pop that shirt off, and we'll start punching.

11:20.746 --> 11:22.771
- Oh, my God. Really?
- Yeah, man.

11:22.848 --> 11:26.340
Every time I'm gonna take...

11:26.418 --> 11:28.352
- Why can't you just take it off?
- Just take it off.

11:28.420 --> 11:30.581
- You're ruining the moment.
- What is with you and the moment?

11:30.656 --> 11:32.146
You know what?
Forget it. Forget it.

11:32.224 --> 11:34.158
- Who do you want to punch you first?
- I don't care.

11:38.730 --> 11:41.927
- That was good.
- Well, you caught me off guard.

11:42.000 --> 11:44.798
That was a big part of it.

11:44.870 --> 11:48.135
- That was the same spot. The same, exact spot.
- Yeah.

11:48.207 --> 11:50.198
Charlie, if we keep this up,
you're gonna be...

11:50.275 --> 11:52.334
the best underground
street fighter ever, bro.

11:54.346 --> 11:55.973
- Okay. Okay. Deandra.
- Just 10 more minutes.

11:56.048 --> 11:59.142
- No, no. That's it. Dee, that's...
- I love it. I need more of it.

11:59.218 --> 12:01.152
It's dangerous.
Enough. Enough.

12:01.220 --> 12:04.519
Come on, what the hell has gotten
into you the last couple of days?

12:04.590 --> 12:06.615
What the hell is that
supposed to mean?

12:06.692 --> 12:09.286
You think I can't do this by myself?
You think I'm on something?

12:09.361 --> 12:10.692
- "On something"?
- Yeah.

12:10.762 --> 12:12.957
- I never said you were on something.
- Then don't. Don't start.

12:13.031 --> 12:15.693
Hey, now we're talkin' here.
She's a killer.

12:15.767 --> 12:17.325
You're goddamn right I'm a killer.

12:17.402 --> 12:19.802
You look like a Holocaust victim
in pageant makeup.

12:19.872 --> 12:22.500
- I will eat your babies, bitch.
- Bring it!

12:22.574 --> 12:25.509
- Nobody's eating babies.
- Hey, you lookin' to spar, little girl?

12:25.577 --> 12:27.545
- No. No fight. She's not ready.
- Oh, I'm ready.

12:27.613 --> 12:29.843
- No, you're not ready.
- I'm ready! Let me eat her babies.

12:29.915 --> 12:32.475
- What about next Friday, huh?
- Yeah. How's Friday?

12:32.551 --> 12:34.815
- You're crazy.
- How's Friday to you?

12:34.887 --> 12:36.718
What's the matter,
"Frankie Fat Hands"?

12:36.788 --> 12:39.222
- You're afraid she's gonna get knocked out just like you did?
- Hey!

12:39.291 --> 12:41.020
- Get this lion off of me here.
- No!

12:41.093 --> 12:43.687
No! You stop it. This is my fight.
Do you understand me?

12:43.762 --> 12:46.526
I'm sick of men getting in my way.
This is my fight. You hear me?

12:46.598 --> 12:49.658
- You hear what I'm saying?
- Maybe we should leave these two alone, huh?

12:49.735 --> 12:52.329
Okay. We'll see you
next Friday, huh?

12:52.404 --> 12:54.804
"Beauty Versus the Beast II."

12:54.873 --> 12:57.603
Come on, Brianna. Here we go.

12:57.676 --> 13:00.110
- You're not ready for this fight.
- Oh, I have an idea, Dad.

13:00.178 --> 13:03.944
Why don't you shut your fat
little monkey face and hold the bag?

13:06.018 --> 13:08.248
I'm gonna paralyze this bitch.

14:48.787 --> 14:51.415
Yes, Dad, I know the fight
is in a few hours, all right?

14:51.490 --> 14:54.186
I'm trying to find
my goddamn headband. Is that okay?

14:54.259 --> 14:57.285
Is it okay with you if I find my headband
before I come down there?

14:57.362 --> 14:59.455
Is that all right with you, Dad? Jesus!

14:59.531 --> 15:01.556
Why didn't we get
the orange one like I said?

15:01.633 --> 15:04.568
This one might as well
be goddamn camouflaged!

15:04.636 --> 15:07.571
Oh, good. Are you happy now?

15:07.639 --> 15:10.005
I just punched a hole in my wall!

15:16.014 --> 15:18.005
Are you sure you're okay, dude?

15:18.083 --> 15:20.017
No, I'm not.

15:20.085 --> 15:22.417
I start thinking, you know, and it makes...

15:22.487 --> 15:25.354
It makes me so angry.

15:29.661 --> 15:31.595
What am I saying?

15:32.831 --> 15:34.765
Okay. Were gonna go...

15:34.833 --> 15:37.063
We're gonna go sign you up
for the fight.

15:37.135 --> 15:39.365
- Yes!
- And you stay here and eat your eggs.

15:39.438 --> 15:42.271
Have the... Have... Make sure
you eat some of the sandwich.

15:42.340 --> 15:45.434
- Yeah, you can just meet us down there, all right?
- Can you meet us later?

15:45.510 --> 15:48.911
Meet you later?
Can I meet you later?

15:48.980 --> 15:51.448
- Are you gonna meet us?
- Yes, I'm gonna meet you there later!

15:51.516 --> 15:53.381
All right.

16:05.797 --> 16:08.630
All right, sign here, here and here.

16:08.700 --> 16:10.725
And what is this?

16:10.802 --> 16:15.034
These are waiver forms in case
your fighter is seriously injured... or killed.

16:15.107 --> 16:18.076
Oh, we don't care about that.
Sign away.

16:18.143 --> 16:20.077
- What's the, uh, fighter's name?
- Clown Baby.

16:20.145 --> 16:22.943
- Clown Ba... Clown Baby?
- Yeah.

16:23.014 --> 16:26.916
- You mean like a baby clown?
- Not a baby clown. A clown ba...

16:26.985 --> 16:29.545
It's like a baby...
It's like a clown that is a baby.

16:29.621 --> 16:33.421
- I said cl... clown baby.
- Mm-mmm. You said baby clown.

16:33.492 --> 16:35.426
- I don't even care.
- Yep.

16:35.494 --> 16:38.395
"Clown Baby"? What in the hell
kind of a name is Clown Baby?

16:38.463 --> 16:41.261
Bro, it's perfect. Nobody's gonna bet
on a guy named Clown Baby.

16:41.333 --> 16:42.766
He's gonna be a huge underdog.

16:42.834 --> 16:46.600
- Which means we stand to make even more money off him.
- Exactly.

16:46.671 --> 16:49.731
- Oh, that's brilliant.
- Hey, pal, 500 bucks on Clown Baby.

16:49.808 --> 16:52.242
Oh, Dennis. 500?
That's all we got, dude.

16:52.310 --> 16:55.939
You saw Charlie.
We turned that kid into an animal.

16:59.684 --> 17:02.778
Oh, yeah? Call me a Holocaust victim?
Say you're prettier than me?

17:02.854 --> 17:04.913
Okay, maybe that part
might be a little bit true.

17:04.990 --> 17:08.016
We'll see how pretty you are
as soon as I punch a hole in your...

17:08.093 --> 17:10.027
Wha...

17:10.095 --> 17:12.029
Where the he...

17:12.097 --> 17:14.361
Who took my shit?

17:14.432 --> 17:16.366
I might have had some.

17:17.435 --> 17:19.494
What did you just say,
you little bitch?

17:21.306 --> 17:24.036
I might have had some
of your pills or whatever.

17:28.647 --> 17:31.081
Oh, yeah?

17:31.149 --> 17:34.482
I am gonna punch a hole
through your face.

17:34.553 --> 17:36.953
I'd like to see you try that.

17:37.022 --> 17:39.252
Yeah?

17:45.063 --> 17:48.328
- Ooh, you're gonna die!
- Oh, I am gonna rip your face off...

17:48.400 --> 17:52.131
- You're gonna die!
- Make a shirt out of it, and I'm gonna wear it.

17:52.204 --> 17:56.834
I'm gonna take one second to take
my shirt off, and then you're gonna die!

18:00.912 --> 18:03.403
What the... Hey, listen, lady.

18:03.481 --> 18:06.382
You wanna beat up on your little boyfriend,
you go do it somewhere else.

18:06.451 --> 18:08.544
Watch the car.

18:19.030 --> 18:21.521
- Dude, where the hell is your fighter?
- He'll be here.

18:21.600 --> 18:24.000
- He'll be here when?
- Soon!

18:24.069 --> 18:27.300
- Okay, you have five minutes to put a fighter in that ring.
- Okay.

18:27.372 --> 18:29.840
Just got off the phone with Charlie.

18:29.908 --> 18:31.842
- Well, where is he?
- He's in jail with Dee.

18:31.910 --> 18:34.378
- What?
- Apparently they got all hopped up on amphetamines...

18:34.446 --> 18:36.539
and beat the shit out of some guy
in front of the bar.

18:36.615 --> 18:39.345
- Amphetamines?
- Yeah, like, steroids or something. I don't know.

18:39.417 --> 18:41.851
- Damn it, Charlie.
- Look at the dude he was supposed to fight.

18:41.920 --> 18:44.548
- He's the scrawniest...
- I know! Charlie would have killed that guy.

18:44.623 --> 18:45.715
We're gonna miss out
on all this money.

18:45.790 --> 18:47.758
- Anybody could kick that guy's ass.
- I know.

18:47.826 --> 18:51.284
Come on. You could kick...
You-You could kick that guy's ass.

18:51.363 --> 18:53.388
You think?

18:53.465 --> 18:56.628
Oh, my God. Yeah. Yeah. Oh, you're,
like, the second toughest guy I know.

18:56.701 --> 18:58.032
I did bash Charlie good a couple times.

18:58.103 --> 18:59.400
- You almost hurt him once.
- With the bottle?

18:59.471 --> 19:00.995
- Yeah, and that's next to impossible.
- That was good.

19:01.072 --> 19:03.006
- You're... You're good.
- I am good.

19:03.074 --> 19:05.167
Yeah.

19:05.243 --> 19:08.838
Tell you what. Um...
Why don't you go stretch out.

19:08.913 --> 19:12.007
I'll talk to the bookie
and let him know that Clown Baby...

19:12.083 --> 19:14.017
has arrived.

19:15.287 --> 19:17.653
- Let's do it.
- All right.

19:17.722 --> 19:19.747
Goddamn it.

19:19.824 --> 19:22.088
- Frankie, what's the deal?
- She got arrested.

19:22.160 --> 19:26.096
- Ah! I knew that skinny bitch would chicken out.
- So we'll never get the fight.

19:26.164 --> 19:28.598
That's a shame, Frankie.
Lot of unanswered questions.

19:28.667 --> 19:32.501
You want your fight? You got your fight.
You and me, right now.

19:32.570 --> 19:35.596
- Well, I... No.
- What? Daddy, you can beat him. Come on.

19:35.674 --> 19:38.199
- You're next.
- It'll be like the old days. I will kill you.

19:38.276 --> 19:40.403
I will knock your nose off your face.

19:40.478 --> 19:42.742
You wanna knock something,
you knock it off of me.

19:42.814 --> 19:44.907
- That's right.
- All right, you got a fight.

19:44.983 --> 19:46.917
Greg, get my gloves.

19:46.985 --> 19:49.453
- I'm sorry, bro.
- Yeah, well, sorry's not gonna get our money back.

19:49.521 --> 19:52.922
- He was so fast.
- You should have moved around a little more and tired him out.

19:52.991 --> 19:54.982
- We have nothing.
- I don't know what to say.

19:55.060 --> 19:58.427
- I gave it my best.
- Yeah. You know what? Your best wasn't good enough.

19:58.496 --> 20:00.657
- Hey, you have the time?
- Aw, not you again.

20:00.732 --> 20:02.723
We don't have any money.
We just lost it all.

20:02.801 --> 20:04.769
- Empty your pockets.
- Hey, meth-head.

20:04.836 --> 20:06.861
Are you listening to me?
We don't have any money.

20:06.938 --> 20:09.429
Do it, or I will kill you both.

20:09.507 --> 20:11.600
Okay, here you go. Look. Empty.

20:11.676 --> 20:13.109
- Now you.
- I don't have anything.

20:13.178 --> 20:14.805
- Do it.
- I don't have...

20:14.879 --> 20:17.575
- Just empty your pockets.
- No. I'm not emptying 'em. I'm not even gonna...

20:17.649 --> 20:19.776
I don't feel like standing
in this alley all night.

20:19.851 --> 20:21.876
- It's a matter of principle.
- A matter of principle?

20:21.953 --> 20:25.719
- I don't feel like standing in an alley
with a meth-head. - I'm gonna stab you, man!

20:25.790 --> 20:28.850
- For the love of God, empty your pockets.
- Okay.

20:32.997 --> 20:35.830
- What the hell is that?
- Give it to me.

20:35.900 --> 20:38.801
You give us a second.

20:40.538 --> 20:42.699
Where did you get that money?

20:43.708 --> 20:45.642
I had to change the bet... a little.

20:45.710 --> 20:48.008
- You bet against me?
- I bet against you.

20:48.079 --> 20:50.343
- Why would you bet against me?
- It was the right move.

20:50.415 --> 20:53.976
- I mean, you got your ass kicked.
- Why wouldn't you tell me?

20:54.052 --> 20:57.021
I could have taken a dive.
I wouldn't have had to get my ass kicked.

20:57.088 --> 20:59.989
Mac, it had to look real.

21:00.058 --> 21:02.288
Were you gonna tell me eventually?

21:04.496 --> 21:06.930
- Yes.
- Yeah?

21:06.998 --> 21:10.365
- I was going to tell you eventually.
- Yeah?

21:10.435 --> 21:13.199
You know what?
Stab this son of a bitch.

21:13.271 --> 21:15.205
Oh, wait a second.
Oh, come on, Mac.

21:15.273 --> 21:17.298
Don't be like that, man.
You would have done the same thing.

21:17.375 --> 21:21.243
Come on, don't act like a baby.

21:21.312 --> 21:23.371
Please don't stab me.

21:23.515 --> 21:26.541
Bash this ugly jerk's face in, Daddy.

21:26.618 --> 21:29.712
- Your last chance to chicken out.
- That ain't gonna happen, Bobby.

21:29.788 --> 21:33.121
- I've been waiting for this for a long time.
- All right, Frankie.

21:33.191 --> 21:35.386
Seeing that we're
a couple of old men here...

21:35.460 --> 21:37.485
I think we should
lay down some ground rules.

21:37.562 --> 21:40.224
Now. Number one.

22:05.490 --> 22:07.822
Holy shit!
